course: dictionary
lesson: 7898
title: Big joy in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a feeling so big that it fills the whole body. Rapture is one of them. It means a feeling of great joy and delight, the kind you get when something wonderful happens. Look for clues around the word: the feeling is strong, not just a small smile.
explain: «Toad went into raptures over motor-cars» tells you a lot. Toad is so thrilled that he cannot keep still. Rapture here means great joy, and went into shows that it is a whole state of excitement, not just a moment of liking something. Try swapping in great joy: Toad went into great joy over motor-cars. It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Mole is in raptures at his first day on the river. That is the same kind of happiness: something new and lovely has made him very excited. The phrase in raptures, or go into raptures, always means very excited and pleased about something.
explain: Be careful with the church meaning. Some Christians, especially in the USA, believe in «the Rapture», when Christ will take believers up to heaven at the end of time. Many other Christians do not hold this belief. In a lesson about joy, the everyday meaning is the one to use.
fact: Rapture means a feeling of great joy and delight.
fact: «In raptures» or «go into raptures» means very excited and pleased about something.
fact: Rapture is usually a noun you cannot count, like joy: you say «great rapture», not «a rapture», in most sentences.
fact: Toad «went into raptures» over motor-cars, and Mole is in raptures at his first day on the river.
fact: In some churches, «the Rapture» is a belief about the end of time, and many Christians do not hold it.
exercise: Toad «went into raptures» over motor-cars. What does rapture mean? | A sleepy yawn | Anger at the noise | A fast walk | *Great joy and delight
exercise: Mole is in raptures at his first day on the river. How is Mole feeling? | Cross and grumpy | *Thrilled and overjoyed | Bored and tired | Frightened of the water
exercise: Which phrase means very excited and pleased about something? | go into a rage | go into hiding | go into the house | *go into raptures
test: Which word is closest in meaning to rapture? | *Delight | Silence | Hunger | Worry
test: What does Toad's rapture show about him? | *He is extremely happy and excited | He is cold and wet | He is angry with the motor-cars | He is bored and sleepy
exam: Which sentence uses rapture correctly? | The rapture was a heavy bag that she carried home | *The children were in raptures when the snow fell and school was closed | The children sat in raptures, sad and sleepy | He was in raptures because he was lost and cold
